{{!-- A glyph in the character header that opens a LIST and carries how long it is: the Judge's
      scales and the Blessed's triquetra.

      ALWAYS a <button>, where the toggle glyphs are a button only on an editable sheet. That
      split is about who may WRITE, and this opens a roster; reading who has been branded or
      marked is not an edit, and the dialog withholds its own add/remove controls from a viewer
      who cannot write. `type="button"` is not optional: the whole sheet is one <form> and a bare
      button submits it.

      The count rides the button as a superscript rather than living only in the tooltip: the one
      thing wanted off this icon at a glance is how many are out there, and a tooltip cannot be
      glanced at. Suppressed at zero — a Judge who has branded nobody sees the scales, not a "0".

      Every tooltip argument is passed to `localize` whichever glyph this is; a key that does not
      name one simply ignores it, which is what lets the two share this markup while saying quite
      different sentences.

      Context:
        stem         the base class; the icon is `<stem>-icon` ("stonetop-condemn")
        active       whether the glyph is lit up (NOT the same as having a count: an oath does not
                     redden the scales, only a brand does)
        activeClass  the modifier worn while it is ("is-branding")
        count        the badge; falsy hides it
        countClass   the badge's class, which does not always follow the stem
        openLabelKey / tooltipKey   i18n keys, the latter picked in getData --}}
<button type="button" class="{{stem}}{{#if active}} {{activeClass}}{{/if}}"
        aria-label="{{localize openLabelKey}}"
        data-tooltip="{{localize tooltipKey brands=brands oaths=oaths count=count}}"
        data-tooltip-direction="UP"><span class="{{stem}}-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{#if count}}<span class="{{countClass}}" aria-hidden="true">{{count}}</span>{{/if}}</button>
